1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,920
Bridge the gap between your current self and your best self.
在当下的自己和想成为的自己之间，搭起一座桥。

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:09,760
So now we are going to make a list of the exact habits and changes that you need to make to get your current self closer to your best self.
现在，列出需要作出的具体习惯和改变，让现在的自己更接近理想的自己。

3
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:13,920
For example here are some changes that I have written down have a set time to sleep to wake up.
例如，我写下的一些改变是：固定睡觉和起床的时间。

4
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:20,880
Create a workout schedule and work out 5 to 6 times a week daily movement create a content schedule and stick to it gratitude journal daily.
制定锻炼计划，每周锻炼五到六次，每天活动；制定并遵守内容日程，每天写感恩日记。

5
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:28,240
Get daily water intake in limit to one coffee a day eat healthy 80 and treat myself 20 keep track of expenses and budget.
达到个人饮水目标，咖啡限制为一天一杯，健康饮食也适度犒劳自己，记录花销和预算。

6
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:32,640
So now out of all those that you have pick three that you really want to prioritize.
现在，从这些事情里选出你真正想优先处理的三项。

7
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:41,160
So you know it's really easy to look at this long list of things that you need to do and work on and be like oh my gosh this is overwhelming like where the heck do I even start.
看到那么长的待办清单，很容易觉得不知所措：天哪，我到底从哪里开始？

8
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:48,880
So that's why I really recommend just choosing three which should be the most important ones that you really want to prioritize because change does not happen in 1 day.
所以我真建议只选三个最重要、最想优先做的事情，因为改变不会一天发生。

9
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:53,520
So once you pick your top three stick to it for 14 days no matter what.
选好最重要的三项后，无论怎样都先坚持十四天。

10
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:59,520
And I promise you when you nail down those three you will gain so much confidence to be able to accomplish the next three.
作者说，做好这三项会让你更有信心去完成接下来的三项。

11
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:03,360
And then the next three and then next three and you just continue to build on that momentum.
然后再接下一组三项，一直借着这股势头向前。

12
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:06,480
When I first started my self improvement journey I chose three things.
刚开始自我提升时，我选了三件事。

13
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:11,160
I chose to work out 5 to 6 times a week gratitude journal daily and get my daily water intake in.
我选的是每周锻炼五到六次、每天写感恩日记、完成个人饮水目标。

14
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:14,800
So I chose those three and I stuck to those girls no matter what okay.
我选了这三项，无论怎样都坚持；原字幕 girls 可能是口语称呼或识别问题，待听辨。

15
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:20,120
No matter how I felt waking up that day no matter how tired I felt unmotivated how badly I wanted to quit.
无论那天醒来心情怎样，多累、多没动力、多想放弃。

16
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:26,480
Then 14 days became a month and then a month became 6 and then 6 became boom we're here now 5 years later.
十四天变成一个月，一个月变成六个月，然后就这样，五年过去了。

17
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:31,280
And after completing those three I just kept on adding new habits and new habits that I wanted to start.
完成这三项后，我就不断增加自己想开始的新习惯。

18
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:35,030
And when I tell you the confidence that you gain from completing those three really works.
完成这三件事所积累的自信，对我确实有帮助。

19
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:39,400
Like after those three I decided I want to be a better student and get the best grades that I can.
之后，我决定成为更好的学生，尽力取得自己能达到的成绩。

20
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:46,640
So that semester I had a 3 2 gpa and then the next semester when I applied myself and I made it my goal to get the highest gpa I can.
那学期我的绩点是3.2；下学期我认真投入，把目标定为拿到力所能及的最高绩点。

21
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:52,640
I got a 3 9 gpa and I stuck to being a good student and getting good grades and I graduated with honors.
后来我拿到3.9，继续认真学习、保持成绩，最后以优异成绩毕业。

22
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:58,320
So yeah it does not take a special person or crazy talent to start okay you just need the willingness to try.
所以，开始并不需要特别的人或惊人天赋，只需要愿意尝试。

23
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:00,800
Rely on your identity not your goals.
依靠对自己身份的认同，而不仅是目标。

24
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:07,360
So these next 14 days when you stick to these three goals that you have it's not going to feel comfortable and you will not feel like doing it some days.
接下来十四天，坚持这三项目标不会一直舒服，有些日子你根本不想做。

25
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:12,470
You will feel tired so something I got from the book atomic habits by james clear another great self help book.
有些日子你会累。接下来这个想法来自 James Clear 的《原子习惯》，也是我喜欢的自助书。

26
00:02:12,480 --> 00:02:20,880
Feeling motivated and being able to achieve all your goals is actually less about the individual goals that you wrote down and it's more about your whole identity.
有动力、实现目标，与其说取决于写下的单个目标，作者认为更取决于整体身份认同。

27
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:24,110
So for example if you tell yourself I am an active person.
例如，你告诉自己：我是个爱活动的人。

28
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:28,880
Getting daily movement in and sticking to a workout routine are both actions that reinforce your identity.
每天动一动、坚持锻炼计划，这两项行动就会强化这种自我认同。

29
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:35,520
Because those two habits are in alignment with that identity so I'm an active person versus I need to get movement in every day.
因为这些习惯与身份认同一致；对比一下“我是爱活动的人”和“我每天需要活动”。

30
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:39,560
If you focus on I need to get daily movement every day that one specific goal.
如果只盯着“我每天得活动”这个单一的具体目标，

31
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:43,440
It might not feel very natural to you because it's not in alignment with your current self.
你也许会觉得不自然，因为它与你目前对自己的认识并不一致。

32
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:53,239
So basically everything that you do from this point on you should do based on the identity of the best version of yourself not the pure motivation of all these little goals that you have.
所以作者建议，从现在起，按你理想中那个自己的身份来行动，而非只靠这些小目标带来的动力。

33
00:02:53,239 --> 00:02:57,720
Have like minded people around you whoever you surround yourself with is who you will become.
身边要有志同道合的人；作者认为，你周围的人会影响你成为什么样的人。

34
00:02:57,720 --> 00:03:03,960
I don't know who needs to hear this but if you are around people that all they do all day is sit around and gossip about other people.
不知道谁需要听到这句话，但如果你身边的人整天只坐着议论别人，

35
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:09,239
They're jealous of other people they don't really have goals for themselves they're just constantly negative they're negative vibe.
嫉妒别人、自己没有目标、总是很消极，充满负面情绪，

36
00:03:09,239 --> 00:03:13,360
They're always jealous of other people do you know those friends that secretly prey on your downfall.
总是嫉妒别人；你知道那种暗地盼你倒霉的朋友吗？原字幕 prey 可能误识别。
